.git
.github
.claude
.spec-flow
docs
specs
epics
*.md

# server/ holds local runtime state (.fabric, libraries, versions, world, mods,
# logs — ~135 MB, all untracked) that was being uploaded as build context on
# every `docker build`. The Dockerfile needs exactly ONE file from here:
# `COPY server/server.properties .`.
#
# ORDER IS LOAD-BEARING: .dockerignore is last-match-wins, so this exclusion
# MUST stay ABOVE the negation below. Moving it after `!server/server.properties`
# makes the exclusion win and breaks the build at that COPY step.
# `server/*` (not `server`) is deliberate — it excludes the directory's contents
# while leaving the directory itself matchable, so the negation can re-include.
server/*
!server/server.properties
sharkengine/.gradle
sharkengine/build
# Fabric dev-client runtime dir created by `./gradlew runClient` (~227 MB of
# untracked assets/natives/logs). Pure local build output like `build/` above;
# the headless `./gradlew build -x test` in the builder stage never reads it.
sharkengine/run
sharkengine/.idea
sharkengine/*.iml
